const faqs=[
 ['How do I convert hourly pay to annual salary?','Multiply your hourly rate by your regular hours per week and paid weeks per year. At $25 an hour for 40 hours a week over 52 weeks, gross annual pay is $52,000.'],
 ['How much is $20 an hour per year?','$20 an hour equals $41,600 a year at 40 hours a week for 52 paid weeks. That is $800 per week and an average of $3,466.67 per month before taxes.'],
 ['How much is $25 an hour per year?','$25 an hour equals $52,000 a year under a 40-hour week and 52 paid weeks. If two weeks are unpaid, the same schedule produces $50,000.'],
 ['How much is $30 an hour per year?','$30 an hour equals $62,400 a year at 40 hours a week for 52 paid weeks. It averages $5,200 a month before taxes and deductions.'],
 ['How much is $50,000 a year per hour?','$50,000 divided by 2,080 scheduled hours equals approximately $24.04 an hour. A different schedule changes that equivalent rate.'],
 ['How many hours are in a full-time work year?','A 40-hour workweek over 52 weeks equals 2,080 scheduled hours. This is a calculation baseline. Paid time off can reduce hours actually worked without reducing an annual salary.'],
 ['Does this calculator include taxes?','No. The results show gross pay before income taxes, insurance, retirement contributions, or other deductions. A paycheck’s net amount will be different.'],
 ['Can I change how many hours I work?','Yes. Enter your regular hours per week and weeks per year. Advanced options include days per week and unpaid time off. Part-time and nonstandard schedules use the same formulas with your own inputs.'],
 ['Can I account for unpaid vacation?','Yes. Enter unpaid weeks off. For hourly, daily, weekly, and biweekly inputs, those weeks reduce annual earnings. For annual and monthly salary inputs, the stated salary stays fixed and the equivalent hourly rate changes.'],
 ['What is the difference between biweekly and semi-monthly pay?','Biweekly means every two weeks, typically 26 checks per year. Semi-monthly means twice each month, or 24 checks per year. The amount per check differs even when annual pay is the same.']
];
